* Using differential mode in ADS1115 at 0x49 I2C, between pins A2 and A3
* Had to remove calls to abs(), or else we would never get negative readings
* Measurements when taking energy from grid, are positive
* Net calculated and measured are approximately the same, measured seems to update much faster than calculated, and measured is higher (more injected energy) than calculated
* The problem is with using RMS to calculate voltage, as that would turn any negative values into positive, hence when drawing current from the grid, we would still see positive numbers
* In fact, issue may be with what the differential mode measures : are we sure it returns a signed voltage and that we can use RMS to calculate net in / out current as for other measurements?
* When consumption is higher than PV production, absolute values rather match, but obviously not the sign (all measurements end up positive)

After all, I am not sure if it is really possible to measure power in both directions reliably using just an SCT-013 and an ADS1115 in differential mode :
- SCT-013 induces an AC votage on its outputs , which is exactly the same no matter the current direction
- Differential ADS1115 does not seem to play a role or help at all in determining current direction (as it only measures voltage +- Volts)
- In any case, at any instant it should still return the absolute (positive) value (as calculated RMS) for either the current pulled from the grid or the current sent to the grid
- But the fact is, as can be seen from picture below :
  - At nightime, measured power drawn from grid is approximately constant (390 W) even upon a significant range of real power consumption (150 - 300 W)
  - When consumption from grid is high, estimated and measured values are similar
  -rw-rw-r-- 1 jdomingo jdomingo 125784 feb 23 20:16 calculated_measured_net_power_comparison.png


So abandoning this attempt to get net metering implemented here will continue to calculate it from individual energy consumers and PV plant generation.


